id: pm-cql43
title: "CodeQL 43: keep worker-bridge debug diagnostics free of raw arguments and stderr"
description: "CodeQL js/clear-text-logging alert43 at tests/helpers/cliWorkerBridge.ts:136 has four SARIF flows from generated temporary global-path data to logged CLI arguments. This is not evidence of a leaked credential. Independently the optional PM_TEST_CLI_BRIDGE_DEBUG=1 sink prints all arguments and captured stderr into test logs. Emit only a fixed failure diagnostic while preserving the entire captured result for deliberate assertions. The harness is excluded from the published package; no actual credential leak or production exposure is established."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 0
tags[1]: security
created_at: "2026-10-06T00:23:55.967Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-06T01:12:18.370Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Real worker synthetic-private-input regression must fail before correction and pass afterward; debug enabled failures emit only a fixed diagnostic; disabled debugging and successful calls stay silent; retain captured status/stdout/stderr and synchronous/fallback contracts; preserve complete exact source coverage and verify main CodeQL retirement.
parent: pm-qwoy
risk: high
confidence: high
expected_result: Automatic bridge debug output contains no arguments stderr or inherited environment values; callers still receive complete captured outcomes.
